# Build context exclusions.
#
# There was no .dockerignore before this, which meant the entire project
# directory -- including .venv/, .git/, and roughly 5 GB of rasters that the
# running app never opens -- was sent to the Docker daemon on every build.
#
# The rule of thumb below: the image needs the code, the trained artefacts the
# app loads at runtime, and the display rasters. It does not need anything
# whose only purpose is to *build* those artefacts.

# ── Environments and VCS ──
.venv/
venv*/
env/
.git/
.gitignore
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ── Editor / OS ──
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Tests and dev tooling (not shipped; CI runs them from the checkout) ──
tests/
requirements-dev.txt
requirements-legacy.txt
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# ── Full-resolution model inputs ────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3.7 GB. The dashboard reads static layers through read_downsampled() at
# 1000 px, so it uses display/ instead (21 MB, built by
# src/make_display_rasters.py). GeoAI_New/ is a *model input* directory, needed
# by align_data.py and susceptibility.py --train, neither of which runs in the
# container.
GeoAI_New/

# 1.3 GB of aligned feature rasters. Consumed by the training and
# feature-derivation pipeline; the app reads the precomputed models/live_model.npz
# instead. Needed only if you rebuild the model inside the image.
data_aligned/

# 874 MB IMD gridded-rainfall archive plus other acquisition caches. The
# forecast ships as models/rainfall_forecast_latest.json (see
# rainfall_forecast.write_snapshot) rather than recomputing from the archive.
data/

# Pre-rewrite intermediates and archives.
archive/
processed/
GeoAI_Data/

# ── Large derived rasters nothing loads at runtime ──
# Note what is deliberately NOT excluded here: outputs/flood_hazard_*.tif.
# .dockerignore applies to the whole build context, so excluding those would
# also starve the `api` stage, which serves them. They stay in the context and
# each stage COPYs only what it needs.
#
# These two, though, no stage needs: susceptibility.tif is an input to
# live_model.build() (the container ships the built live_model.npz instead),
# and the uncertainty surface is only read by the offline evaluation scripts.
outputs/susceptibility_uncertainty.tif
outputs/susceptibility.tif
outputs/susceptibility.tif.aux.xml

# ── Superseded model binaries (docs/artefacts.md) ──
# 245 MB of archived Keras/PyTorch U-Net weights. Nothing in the active
# pipeline loads these; the shipped model is the gradient-boosted
# susceptibility surface baked into live_model.npz.
models/*.h5
models/*.pth

# ── Reports and scratch ──
evaluation/
docs/
*.log
*.tmp
*.aux.xml
*.lck
sentinel_data/
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
